# Normalize line endings to LF for text files, so Windows/Linux/Mac
# clones all see the same bytes and nobody gets the "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" warning going forward. Repo-level fix rather than
# relying on everyone's local core.autocrlf -- this takes effect for
# any future clone regardless of local git config, since
# .gitattributes overrides autocrlf for matched paths.
#
# IMPORTANT: text=auto's own binary-detection heuristic got a real
# file wrong once already while building this list -- it misjudged
# wasm/cp400bas.rom (a raw CoCo ROM image) as text and would have
# altered 118 lines' worth of actual ROM bytes on commit. Caught by
# comparing the staged blob's hash against HEAD's before committing,
# not by trusting the "nothing looks different" surface impression.
# Every binary format actually present in this repo (confirmed via
# `file` against every tracked path, not guessed at) is listed
# explicitly below so none of them are left to that heuristic again.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Compiled/binary artifacts
*.wasm    binary
*.rom     binary
*.ROM     binary
*.bin     binary
*.raw     binary
*.ccc     binary
*.zip     binary
*.pem     binary
*.key     binary
*.xls     binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.xcf     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.icns    binary
*.pdf     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.info    binary

# Windows resource file with an unusual encoding (ISO-8859 with NEL
# line terminators, not plain LF) -- marking binary rather than
# guessing at how to normalize it correctly means git leaves it
# completely alone, zero risk, at the minor cost of not getting
# line-based diffs on a single pristine-upstream file we don't edit.
*.rc      binary
